refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public static Time\DurationTime\Duration::fromIso8601DurationString stringspecification
Creates a non-negative duration from the time part of an ISO 8601 duration specification, such as PT1H30M.

&reftitle.errors;
This method throws a Time\TimeException in the following cases:
specification cannot be parsed as an ISO 8601 duration specification contains a date designator (Y, M, W or D) specification is a date/time or a time interval rather than a duration the resulting duration exceeds the maximum length of a duration

  &reftitle.examples;

   Time\Duration::fromIso8601DurationString example


<?php
var_dump(Time\Duration::fromIso8601DurationString('PT1H30M'));

var_dump(Time\Duration::fromIso8601DurationString('PT90S')->seconds);

try {
    Time\Duration::fromIso8601DurationString('P1D');
} catch (Time\TimeException $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}

try {
    Time\Duration::fromIso8601DurationString('PT0.5S');
} catch (Time\TimeException $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


